Reach the Thread from x86_64 compiled code through bionic's TLS slot in the ANDRUNA build.

The optimizing compiler and the JNI compiler emit Thread accesses as
gs()->insn(Address::Absolute(offset, no_rip)). Under ANDRUNA, gs() loads
the Thread* from %fs:0x38 (TLS_SLOT_ART_THREAD_SELF) into R11 (TMP, which
the code generators reserve) and the next instruction's absolute operand
is encoded as [R11 + offset]. Two JNI sites where R11 is an input of the
instruction pass another register: StoreStackPointerToThread (RAX) and
TryToTransitionFromRunnableToNative (a callee-save scratch register).
Without ANDRUNA, gs() is the GS segment prefix as before.

